WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.497
The battle above was so loud, the earth seemed to move.

2
00:00:04.498 --> 00:00:08.871
The children heard screams of terror and Indian war cries.

3
00:00:08.872 --> 00:00:14.201
Stunned, they stopped packing for their trip and opened their mouths in alarm.

4
00:00:14.202 --> 00:00:20.511
They fell silent as stones, listening for a clue to how the battle was going.

5
00:00:20.512 --> 00:00:25.375
For the Indians, however, the attack was not a complete surprise.

6
00:00:25.376 --> 00:00:37.160
From the moment the pirates had landed on the island, and one had stepped on a dry stick, the Indians had known the pirates were there and expected a fight.

7
00:00:37.161 --> 00:00:40.312
They had even sent scouts out to investigate.

8
00:00:40.313 --> 00:00:44.579
But the Indians were used to sneaking up on an enemy camp at dawn.

9
00:00:44.580 --> 00:00:48.846
Everyone knew this was how battles with Indians were supposed to go.

10
00:00:48.847 --> 00:00:54.501
So the Indians waited, expecting the pirates to stop and set up camp.

11
00:00:54.502 --> 00:00:57.622
The cunning Captain Hook fooled them.

12
00:00:57.623 --> 00:01:03.135
It was the pirates who snuck up on the Indians, and they attacked late in the night.

13
00:01:03.136 --> 00:01:09.182
Surprised, the Indian warriors grabbed their weapons and yelled out their war cries.

14
00:01:09.183 --> 00:01:16.625
They had promised to guard the children's home, and they fought bravely to the end. But they were beaten.

15
00:01:16.626 --> 00:01:23.380
Only Tiger Lily and a few Indian warriors survived the battle. And they quickly fled.

16
00:01:23.381 --> 00:01:27.942
Hook watched the pirates wipe their swords and catch their breath.

17
00:01:27.943 --> 00:01:35.100
"Well done, men," he grinned. "But the night's work is not over yet."

18
00:01:35.101 --> 00:01:40.437
"What? What does he mean?" said the pirates to one another.

19
00:01:40.438 --> 00:01:47.160
"You see," Hook went on, "The Indians aren't really who I was after.

20
00:01:47.161 --> 00:01:50.871
I want to capture Wendy and the Lost Boys.

21
00:01:50.872 --> 00:01:56.517
And most of all, I want the blood of Peter Pan!"

22
00:01:56.518 --> 00:02:02.750
Peter was such a little boy that it is hard to imagine why Hook hated him so much.

23
00:02:02.751 --> 00:02:07.719
True, Peter had cut off Hook's hand and thrown it to the crocodile.

24
00:02:07.720 --> 00:02:11.966
But it was Peter's pride that really made Hook's blood boil.

25
00:02:11.967 --> 00:02:17.785
"How can a boy so young be so boastful?" he wondered.

26
00:02:17.786 --> 00:02:22.735
Just thinking about it made his iron claw twitch.

27
00:02:22.736 --> 00:02:28.497
The question now for Hook was how to get the pirates down into Peter's underground home.

28
00:02:28.498 --> 00:02:33.635
He knew his pirates were too big to fit into the small boys' hollow trees.

29
00:02:33.636 --> 00:02:38.072
And they would never squeeze through the tunnels to the underground home.

30
00:02:38.073 --> 00:02:44.274
Hook looked over at his men and said quietly, "Now which of you is the skinniest?"

31
00:02:44.275 --> 00:02:49.032
Down below, Peter, Wendy, and the boys were anxious.

32
00:02:49.033 --> 00:02:55.297
"The noise has finally stopped," Peter said. "The battle must be over."

33
00:02:55.298 --> 00:03:00.402
"Yes, but which side has won?" asked Wendy, worried.

34
00:03:00.403 --> 00:03:03.326
Their lives depended on the answer.

35
00:03:03.327 --> 00:03:08.812
"If the Indians have won," answered Peter, "they will beat their drum.

36
00:03:08.813 --> 00:03:12.568
It is their victory signal. So we must listen."

37
00:03:12.569 --> 00:03:17.323
At this, Wendy and the children all went silent again.

38
00:03:17.324 --> 00:03:23.598
Meanwhile, looking for a place to rest, Smee found the Indians' drum and sat on it.

39
00:03:23.599 --> 00:03:29.475
"No one will hear this drum again," he said to himself, pleased.

40
00:03:29.476 --> 00:03:36.054
But to his surprise, Hook whispered, "Smee, beat the drum."

41
00:03:36.055 --> 00:03:43.810
Captain Hook was just as clever as Peter, and Smee smiled when he understood what his sneaky captain was up to.

42
00:03:43.811 --> 00:03:48.826
Smee beat the drum, and the sound rang through the woods.

43
00:03:48.827 --> 00:03:54.376
Below ground the boys yelled, "It's an Indian victory!"

44
00:03:54.377 --> 00:03:58.973
They let out a cheer so loud that the pirates heard it above.

45
00:03:58.974 --> 00:04:05.272
The boys repeated their good-byes to Peter and prepared to come up through the hollow trees.

46
00:04:05.273 --> 00:04:11.203
Above them the pirates smiled evilly at each other and rubbed their hands.

47
00:04:11.204 --> 00:04:15.684
Hook silently motioned each pirate to pick a hollow tree and watch it.

48
00:04:15.685 --> 00:04:24.436
In this way, they would catch the boys as they emerged from the ground.

